  "title": "Lab results on a date of service that contains the DST fall-back",
  "scenario": "A clinician asks for all chemistry results drawn on the date of service 2024-11-03 (the day US clocks fall back from EDT to EST at 02:00 local). Results come from interfaces that send UTC instants, local offsets, a foreign offset, an offset-less local time, a day-only date, a month-only date and one timed collection period. You are checking which resources each query returns.",
  "server_timezone": "America/New_York",
  "why_hard": "The local day 2024-11-03 is 25 hours long: [2024-11-03T04:00Z, 2024-11-04T05:00Z). Using a single fixed offset for the day gets one end wrong. 01:00-01:59 local occurs twice (-04:00 then -05:00). Search values at minute precision are one-minute intervals; target instants at second precision are one-second intervals.",
